READ_ME {
A library on `no-number = "stops"` whose ITMT divides a `bin` by zero inside
one of its own functions. Building this alone is refused: the run the compiler
watches stops there, both ways it has of running it.
}
LIBRARY {
    fn.export.bin64 'ratio' [bin64 'a', bin64 'b'] { give ['a' / 'b']; }
}
ITMT {
    print.stdout[ratio[*1*, *0*] \n];
}
